#Loops (while, do-while, for)

## 1] while Loop

### What it is

Executes a block of code repeatedly **as long as the condition is true**.

###  When to use

* When the number of iterations is **not known beforehand**
* Condition is checked **before execution**

###  Syntax

while (condition) {
    // code executes
}


## 2] do-while Loop

###  What it is

Executes a block of code at least once, then repeats while condition is true.

### 📌 When to use

* When the code must run **at least once**
* Condition is checked **after execution**

###  Syntax

do {
    // code executes
} while (condition);


## 3]for Loop

###  What it is

A loop used when the number of iterations is **known beforehand**.

### When to use

* When you know how many times to run the loop

###  Syntax

for (initialization; condition; update) {
    // code executes
}


## Key Components of for Loop

* Initialization → starting point
* Condition → loop runs while true
* Update → increment/decrement




## while vs do-while

| Feature         | while            | do-while             |
| --------------- | ---------------- | -------------------- |
| Execution       | 0 or more times  | At least once        |
| Condition check | Before execution | After execution      |
| Use case        | General loops    | Menu-driven programs |



## for vs while

| Feature   | for loop         | while loop         |
| --------- | ---------------- | ------------------ |
| Use case  | Known iterations | Unknown iterations |
| Structure | Compact          | More flexible      |

