## Infinite Loop

###  What it is

A loop that never ends because the condition is always true.

### Examples

while (true) {
    // infinite loop
}

for (;;) {
    // infinite loop
}


## Loop Control Statements

### break

* Terminates the loop immediately

for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    if (i == 3) {
        break;
    }
    System.out.println(i);
}

### continue

* Skips the current iteration

for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    if (i == 3) {
        continue;
    }
    System.out.println(i);
}


## Best Practices

* Use `for` loop when iterations are known
* Use `while` loop when condition-based repetition is needed
* Use `do-while` when at least one execution is required
* Avoid infinite loops unless intentionally used
* Keep loop conditions simple and readable
